<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρο-κτᾰσία</span></b> , ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτείνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slaughter of men</i> in battle, mostly in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παύσασθαι . . Ἄρην ἀνδροκτασιάων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.909
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχας τ᾽ ἀνδροκτασίας τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.237
				</span></i>
			, etc.: personified, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				228
			</span></i>: in sg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδροκτασίης ὕπο
			λυγρῆς</span> by reason of sad <i>homicide,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.86
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1359.1.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				693
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
